## Objective

Build a Bank Account model that demonstrates encapsulation, private state, getters, controlled mutation, validation, constructor initialization, and static class-level information.

```dart
class BankAccount {
  final String accountId;

  double _balance;

  static const double minimumOpeningBalance = 100;

  BankAccount({
    required this.accountId,
    double initialBalance = minimumOpeningBalance,
  }) : _balance = initialBalance {
    if (initialBalance < minimumOpeningBalance) {
      throw ArgumentError(
        'Opening balance must be at least $minimumOpeningBalance.',
      );
    }
  }

  double get balance => _balance;

  void deposit(double amount) {
    if (amount <= 0) {
      throw ArgumentError('Deposit amount must be greater than zero.');
    }

    _balance += amount;
  }

  void withdraw(double amount) {
    if (amount <= 0) {
      throw ArgumentError('Withdrawal amount must be greater than zero.');
    }

    if (amount > _balance) {
      throw StateError('Insufficient balance.');
    }

    _balance -= amount;
  }
}
```

The lesson should also include the ShoppingCart exercise demonstrating controlled access to a mutable collection.
